# Screen-local AG Grid

List screens use **`ag-grid-angular`** directly in the template with shared helpers from `frontend/src/styles/ag-grid-theme.ts`. Do not use a grid wrapper component.

See **`settings-user-management-table`** (primary reference) and **`master-company-table`** in `screen-reference.mdc`.

```html
<div class="flex shrink-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-b border-border px-3 py-2.5 sm:flex-nowrap sm:px-4 sm:py-3">
  <!-- search input + toolbar app-button actions -->
</div>

<div class="min-h-0 flex-1">
  <ag-grid-angular
    class="h-full w-full"
    [theme]="theme"
    [rowData]="rows()"
    [columnDefs]="columnDefs"
    [defaultColDef]="defaultColDef"
    [context]="gridContext"
    [loading]="isLoading()"
    [pagination]="true"
    [paginationPageSize]="pageSize"
    [paginationPageSizeSelector]="false"
    rowSelection="single"
    [suppressCellFocus]="true"
    [animateRows]="false"
    overlayNoRowsTemplate="No rows found"
    (gridReady)="onGridReady($event)"
  />
</div>
```

```ts
import { AgGridAngular } from 'ag-grid-angular';
import type { ColDef, GridApi, GridReadyEvent } from 'ag-grid-community';
import {
  actionColumnDef,
  GridActionContext,
  qlDefaultColDef,
  qlGridTheme,
  qlPageSize,
  serialNoColumnDef,
  statusColumnDef,
} from '../../../styles/ag-grid-theme';
```

## Setup checklist

- AG Grid modules are registered once in `frontend/src/main.ts`.
- Style search/toolbar with inline Tailwind in the template (no grid wrapper SCSS).
- Use `qlGridTheme`, `qlDefaultColDef`, `qlPageSize`.
- Track `gridApi` and a `quickFilterText` signal; call `gridApi.setGridOption('quickFilterText', …)` on search input.
- Build columns with `serialNoColumnDef`, `statusColumnDef`, `actionColumnDef`.
- Pass edit/delete handlers via `[context]` (`GridActionContext`).
